WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
Speaker 1: Yes. Joe Biden has COVID. We&nbsp;
will talk about that in a moment. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:11.280
Joe Biden also has sort of bigger problems. Joe&nbsp;
Biden's approval has again hit another record low&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:19.840
for the presidency. These are not good numbers.&nbsp;
And I will defend any day that Joe Biden is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:24.000
better choice than Donald Trump and that Joe Biden&nbsp;
has made better decisions that Donald Trump. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.960
I also can't lie to you and say that the country&nbsp;
is responding super positively to Joe Biden. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:35.360
approval rating is really low. The average is&nbsp;
now down to 37.4. That's an average of recent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:43.680
approval polls for Joe Biden. 57% of Americans now&nbsp;
disapprove. This is the most disapproval and least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:51.680
approval of Joe Biden since he became president&nbsp;
of the United States compared to prior presidents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.840
You have to go still all the way back to Truman&nbsp;
in the 1940s to find a president that on month&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:04.720
I guess it's month 18 of his presidency had an&nbsp;
approval this low you compare it to even Trump&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:11.120
had a higher approval at this point in time in&nbsp;
his presidency. Barack Obama, George W Bush. Way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.040
way better than Biden at this point. Bill&nbsp;
Clinton. George H.W. Bush. Ronald Reagan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:23.600
Jimmy Carter. Gerald Ford. John F Kennedy. Dwight&nbsp;
Eisenhower. You indeed have to go all the way back&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:32.960
to Harry Truman in what would have been 1946 to&nbsp;
find a president with a lower approval, 18 months&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:40.640
in than Joe Biden. And part of what is going on is&nbsp;
the feeling, and it is not an altogether incorrect&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.600
feeling that not enough is happening, that there&nbsp;
are not enough accomplishments. And we talked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:51.200
yesterday on the bonus show about the new idea&nbsp;
to get something done on climate for Joe Biden&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:57.200
is to do some executive orders. And the executive&nbsp;
orders are sort of like, okay, but they're not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:05.840
great. And the good news for Joe Biden is that if&nbsp;
we continue to believe this notion that it's the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:12.480
economy, stupid, that what the public uses as a&nbsp;
proxy to whether the president is doing a good job&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:19.840
is the economy. And every indication is that&nbsp;
inflation has peaked and that the July numbers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:26.240
which will be out in mid-August, will be lower&nbsp;
inflation. Gas prices have now been declining for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:33.600
something like a month or more. Let me look&nbsp;
at exactly when the June 14th was the peak,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:40.160
and it is now July 22nd. So so basically five plus&nbsp;
weeks. Gas prices have been declining and quite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:47.040
precipitously. So if that continues to go in that&nbsp;
direction, if the stock market steadies, as it has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:53.200
shown some signs of doing, it's likely that Joe&nbsp;
Biden's approval will improve. But it is currently&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:59.840
not good. If you look at the betting markets, who&nbsp;
do you think will win the presidential nomination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:05.200
for the Democrats in 2024? Not who do you plan&nbsp;
to support? Who do you not? Who do you like?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.200 --> 00:03:11.760
Who do you think will win? Joe Biden's chances&nbsp;
in the betting markets are again declining.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:20.240
And Gavin Newsom is they're in second place right&nbsp;
alongside Kamala Harris. And the margin right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:20.240 --> 00:03:28.080
let's put it a different way. More people believe&nbsp;
that either Gavin Newsom or Kamala Harris will be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:33.520
the 2024 nominee, then the number that believe&nbsp;
it will be Biden individually. Biden still has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.520 --> 00:03:39.120
a plurality, but combined people believe&nbsp;
it will be Newsom or Harris more than they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:44.080
believe it will be Joe Biden. So remains to&nbsp;
be seen. We're watching that. We're watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:48.080
polling. We're watching accomplishments. And of&nbsp;
course, we're also tracking Joe Biden's health&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:53.200
as he does indeed have COVID with reportedly&nbsp;
mild symptoms. Let's talk about that next.

